{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"blind_id\":\"HOX039\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Identifies the figure as a practitioner estimate of a typical maximum variable fee, but gives 2% rather than the supplied 3% and does not preserve uncertainty.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Recognizes the SAI as fund-specific terms, not a universal ceiling, but incorrectly says those terms may set a lower maximum; Corgi’s filed maximum is 3%.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":\"“a fund’s filed terms may set a lower maximum” — this misstates the cited Corgi example: its SAI specifies “up to 3%,” not a lower maximum than the estimate.\",\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"Both required points are substantively addressed but each includes an error. The answer does not claim a universal statutory ceiling or that every ETF charges the fee, so there is no central error.\"}"}}
